     "name": "Rahul",
     "person_id": "p-rahul",
     "color_idx": 1,
     "utterance_count": 12,
     "talk_time_s": 99.3
    },
    {
     "track": "S3",
     "label": "Speaker 3",
     "name": "Meera",
     "person_id": "p-meera",
     "color_idx": 2,
     "utterance_count": 12,
     "talk_time_s": 88.7
    },
    {
     "track": "S4",
     "label": "Speaker 4",
     "name": "Arjun",
     "person_id": "p-arjun",
     "color_idx": 3,
     "utterance_count": 7,
     "talk_time_s": 53.6
    }
   ],
   "utterances": [
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-000",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 0,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 0.6,
     "t_end": 8.9,
     "text": "Okay, let's start. Today we lock the self-serve pricing for Kitepost, so sales can quote it and Arjun's team can build billing against it.",
     "confidence": 0.958
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-001",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 1,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 9.5,
     "t_end": 19.95,
     "text": "Before we get into tiers, keep one number in mind. Our cost per tracked shipment is about 1.8 rupees, once you include WhatsApp messages and map lookups.",
     "confidence": 0.955
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-002",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 2,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 20.65,
     "t_end": 27.7,
     "text": "Fine. So the proposal on the table is three tiers: Starter, Growth and Enterprise, with Enterprise staying sales-led.",
     "confidence": 0.967
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-003",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 3,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 28.3,
     "t_end": 38.56,
     "text": "And I want Starter at 3,999 rupees a month. Trackwise charges small shippers 3,999, and they are who we lose deals to.",
     "confidence": 0.944
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-004",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 4,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 39.06,
     "t_end": 50.28,
     "text": "At 3,999 with fifteen hundred shipments included, a busy Starter account runs at about 32 percent margin. I can't sign off on that.",
     "confidence": 0.934
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-005",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 5,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 50.88,
     "t_end": 57.88,
     "text": "Most Starter accounts won't come close to fifteen hundred. The Saffron Basket pilot averaged around nine hundred shipments a month.",
     "confidence": 0.973
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-006",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 6,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 58.38,
     "t_end": 66.07,
     "text": "Saffron Basket is one customer. I'd rather price for the busy accounts and be pleasantly surprised by the quiet ones.",
     "confidence": 0.945
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-007",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 7,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 66.97,
     "t_end": 77.19,
     "text": "Can I add the engineering angle? If we cap included shipments and charge overage, the base price matters less, because heavy users pay their own way.",
     "confidence": 0.949
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-008",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 8,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 77.79,
     "t_end": 83.24,
     "text": "That's where I was going too. Rahul, what overage rate per shipment keeps us safe on margin?",
     "confidence": 0.962
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-009",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 9,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 83.84,
     "t_end": 91.51,
     "text": "Four rupees per extra shipment. That's more than double our cost, and still cheaper than what Trackwise charges for overage.",
     "confidence": 0.985
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-010",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 10,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 92.01,
     "t_end": 97.98,
     "text": "Four rupees is fine. Customers accept overage if the dashboard shows it to them before the invoice does.",
     "confidence": 0.966
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-011",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 11,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 98.68,
     "t_end": 105.76,
     "text": "Which means we need a usage meter in the product. Right now we only count shipments in the nightly billing job.",
     "confidence": 0.959
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-012",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 12,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 106.56,
     "t_end": 117.16,
     "text": "Okay, let me propose something concrete. Starter at 4,999 rupees a month, fifteen hundred shipments included, and four rupees per shipment after that.",
     "confidence": 0.983
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-013",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 13,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 117.86,
     "t_end": 125.26,
     "text": "I still think 4,999 makes the first sales call harder. But with a visible usage meter, I can sell it.",
     "confidence": 0.93
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-014",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 14,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 125.76,
     "t_end": 134.36,
     "text": "I'm comfortable with 4,999. That keeps a busy Starter account at around 46 percent margin.",
     "confidence": 0.977
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-015",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 15,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 134.96,
     "t_end": 144.01,
     "text": "Then that's decided. We'll go with the 4,999 rupee Starter tier, with fifteen hundred shipments and four rupee overage.",
     "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-016",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 16,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 144.81,
     "t_end": 152.09,
     "text": "Noted on Starter. And for the Growth tier, are we still holding at 14,999 a month?",
     "confidence": 0.984
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-017",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 17,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 152.59,
     "t_end": 160.8,
     "text": "Yes, 14,999 for ten thousand shipments, plus WhatsApp delivery updates and two warehouse locations.",
     "confidence": 0.951
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-018",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 18,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 161.4,
     "t_end": 167.42,
     "text": "Monsoon Apparel asked about Growth last week. They run three warehouses, so two locations won't cover them.",
     "confidence": 0.975
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-019",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 19,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 167.92,
     "t_end": 174.12,
     "text": "Then Monsoon is an Enterprise conversation. Let's not bend the Growth tier around a single account.",
     "confidence": 0.953
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-020",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 20,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 174.72,
     "t_end": 179.31,
     "text": "Fair enough. I'll take Monsoon Apparel through the Enterprise proposal next week instead.",
     "confidence": 0.984
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-021",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 21,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 180.21,
     "t_end": 185.33,
     "text": "Next, annual billing. Meera, you wanted twenty percent off for annual plans, right?",
     "confidence": 0.962
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-022",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 22,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 185.83,
     "t_end": 193.05,
     "text": "Twenty percent. Annual prepay is how we get cash up front from small businesses, and twenty is what makes people actually choose it.",
     "confidence": 0.947
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-023",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 23,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 193.55,
     "t_end": 201.28,
     "text": "Twenty is too much. At twenty percent off, the Starter margin gets thin again. I'd cap the annual discount at fifteen.",
     "confidence": 0.946
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-024",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 24,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 201.78,
     "t_end": 206.67,
     "text": "Fifteen percent doesn't move anyone. Nobody switches to annual billing for fifteen percent.",
     "confidence": 0.985
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-025",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 25,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 207.27,
     "t_end": 215.39,
     "text": "Our own data says otherwise. Forty percent of the Saffron Basket cohort picked annual billing at only twelve percent off.",
     "confidence": 0.947
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-026",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 26,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 216.09,
     "t_end": 222.16,
     "text": "Is that cohort big enough to trust, though? If I remember right, it was only about thirty accounts.",
     "confidence": 0.934
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-027",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 27,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 222.66,
     "t_end": 229.34,
     "text": "It was 34 accounts. Small, I agree, but it's the only real annual billing data we have so far.",
     "confidence": 0.96
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-028",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 28,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 230.14,
     "t_end": 238.1,
     "text": "I'm going to side with Rahul on this one. The annual discount is fifteen percent, and we revisit it after ninety days of real data.",
     "confidence": 0.94
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-029",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 29,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 238.7,
     "t_end": 243.9,
     "text": "Okay. I'm not thrilled, but fifteen percent with a review at ninety days is something I can live with.",
     "confidence": 0.943
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-030",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 30,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 244.8,
     "t_end": 252.8,
     "text": "On the build side, the usage meter is the real blocker. Billing can't go live without it, and sales can't demo overage.",
     "confidence": 0.933
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-031",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 31,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 253.4,
     "t_end": 259.53,
     "text": "Arjun, can you ship the usage meter by Friday? Almost everything else on the launch plan depends on it.",
     "confidence": 0.978
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-032",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 32,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 260.13,
     "t_end": 266.98,
     "text": "Friday works. I'll have it on staging Thursday night, with a warning banner at ninety percent of the plan limit.",
     "confidence": 0.987
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-033",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 33,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 267.68,
     "t_end": 276.06,
     "text": "For sales, I need a revised deck with the new tiers. Saffron Basket's renewal call is on Friday, so I'll send them the revised deck by Thursday.",
     "confidence": 0.933
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-034",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 34,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 276.76,
     "t_end": 286.5,
     "text": "And I'll set up the billing plans in Razorpay by Wednesday: monthly and annual for both Starter and Growth. Enterprise stays on manual invoices.",
     "confidence": 0.988
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-035",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 35,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 287.3,
     "t_end": 292.51,
     "text": "Thanks, Rahul. Now the launch date. I want self-serve live on Monday, November second.",
     "confidence": 0.956
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-036",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 36,
     "speaker": "S4",
     "speaker_name": "Arjun",
     "t_start": 293.11,
     "t_end": 301.19,
     "text": "November second is tight but doable, if the pricing page is final by next week. We need the copy to build the signup flow.",
     "confidence": 0.943
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-037",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 37,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 301.69,
     "t_end": 308.46,
     "text": "That one's on me. I'll draft the pricing page and the FAQ by Monday, including worked overage examples.",
     "confidence": 0.988
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-038",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 38,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 309.06,
     "t_end": 318.7,
     "text": "Put a real example in the FAQ. Two thousand shipments on Starter comes to 6,999 rupees in total, and people should see that math.",
     "confidence": 0.931
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-039",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 39,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 319.3,
     "t_end": 325.0,
     "text": "Good, that example goes in. So we're agreed: self-serve launches on Monday, November second.",
     "confidence": 0.965
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-040",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 40,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 325.7,
     "t_end": 333.7,
     "text": "One risk on that date. GST invoicing through Razorpay needs our new tax registration, and that isn't confirmed yet.",
     "confidence": 0.971
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-041",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 41,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 334.2,
     "t_end": 339.31,
     "text": "Rahul, can you chase the tax registration and confirm it either way by next Tuesday?",
     "confidence": 0.956
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-042",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 42,
     "speaker": "S2",
     "speaker_name": "Rahul",
     "t_start": 339.81,
     "t_end": 348.13,
     "text": "Yes, I'll confirm the GST registration by next Tuesday. If it slips, we launch with manual invoices for the first week.",
     "confidence": 0.988
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-043",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 43,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 348.73,
     "t_end": 359.27,
     "text": "Let me recap the decisions. Starter is 4,999 with fifteen hundred shipments, the annual discount is fifteen percent, and we launch on November second.",
     "confidence": 0.942
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-044",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 44,
     "speaker": "S3",
     "speaker_name": "Meera",
     "t_start": 359.87,
     "t_end": 372.02,
     "text": "And the owners: Arjun has the usage meter by Friday, I have the Saffron Basket deck by Thursday, Rahul has Razorpay by Wednesday and GST by Tuesday, and Priya has the pricing page by Monday.",
     "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
     "id": "u-demo-pricing-review-045",
     "meeting_id": "demo-pricing-review",
     "seq": 45,
     "speaker": "S1",
     "speaker_name": "Priya",
     "t_start": 372.62,
     "t_end": 378.77,
     "text": "That's it. Thanks, everyone, and please use the pricing channel for anything that changes before launch.",
     "confidence": 0.967
    }
   ],
